% GROUP C -- Off-path / helper-thread work on real hardware.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------

% *** STRONGEST MECHANISTIC CORROBORATION AVAILABLE ***
% MICRO 2025. Software-only helper-thread prefetching on real systems. Their
% stated key challenge is TIMELINESS -- the helper thread must get far enough
% ahead but not too far -- and they needed a cheap hardware-supported
% synchronisation primitive because OS synchronisation was too expensive.
%
% That is precisely our dispatch-latency finding, reached independently in a
% different subsystem: off-path work succeeds or fails on whether the
% dispatch/synchronisation cost is small relative to the latency being hidden.
% They found a primitive cheap enough; inside the UVM fault handler, we did
% not. Cite where the 5.598us dispatch latency and the 1,685-1,894x
% load-dependent blowup are introduced.
